 it shares a card type with the card exiled this way. (Artifact, creature, enchantment, instant, land, planeswalker, sorcery, and tribal are card types.)', '{2}, Sacrifice Limestone Golem: Target player draws a card.', '{2}, {T}, Sacrifice Darkwater Egg: Add {U}{B}. Draw a card.', '{2}, {T}, Sacrifice Mossfire Egg: Add {R}{G}. Draw a card.', '{2}, {T}, Sacrifice Shadowblood Egg: Add {B}{R}. Draw a card.', '{2}, {T}, Sacrifice Skycloud Egg: Add {W}{U}. Draw a card.', '{2}, {T}, Sacrifice Sungrass Egg: Add {G}{W}. Draw a card.', "{2}{B}, Discard a card: Face of Fear gains fear until end of turn. (It can't be blocked except by artifact creatures and/or black creatures.)", '{2}{B}, Sacrifice a creature: Target creature gets -2/-2 until end of turn.\\n{2}{B}, Exile a creature card from your graveyard: Target creature gets -2/-2 until end of turn.', '{2}{B}: Infected Vermin deals 1 damage to each creature and each player.\\nThreshold — {3}{B}: Infected Vermin deals 3 damage to each creature and each player. Activate only if seven or more cards are in your graveyard.', "{2}{G}, {T}: Target creature gets +X/+X until end of turn, where X is that creature's power.", '{2}{R}, Sacrifice Barbarian Lunatic: It deals 2 damage to target creature.', '{3}, {T}: Exile target card from a graveyard.\\n{1}, Sacrifice Steamclaw: Exile target card from a graveyard.', "{3}{G}, {T}: Reveal the top card of your library. If it's a creature card, put it onto the battlefield. Otherwise, put it into your graveyard.", '{3}{U}, Exile Shifty Doppelganger: You may put a creature card from your hand onto the battlefield. If you do, that creature gains haste until end of turn. At the beginning of the next end step, sacrifice that creature. If you do, return Shifty Doppelganger to the battlefield.', '{B}, Discard a card: Fledgling Imp gains flying until end of turn.', "{B}, Discard a card: Regenerate Dirty Wererat.\\nThreshold — As long as seven or more cards are in your graveyard, Dirty Wererat gets +2/+2 and can't block.", "{G}, Discard a card: Crashing Centaur gains trample until end of turn.\\nThreshold — As long as seven or more cards are in your graveyard, Crashing Centaur gets +2/+2 and has shroud. (It can't be the target of spells or abilities.)", '{G}, {T}, Sacrifice Druid Lyrist: Destroy target enchantment.', '{G}, {T}: Target creature gets +2/+2 until end of turn.', '{G}{G}: Still Life becomes a 4/3 Centaur creature in addition to its other types until end of turn.', '{R}, Discard a card at random: Frenetic Ogre gets +3/+0 until end of turn.', '{R}, Discard a card at random: Pardic Swordsmith gets +2/+0 until end of turn.', '{R}, Sacrifice a land: Magma Vein deals 1 damage to each creature without flying.', '{T}, Exile any number of cards from your graveyard: Target creature gets -X/-X until end of turn, where X is the number of cards exiled this way.', "{T}, Exile two cards from your graveyard and Zombie Assassin: Destroy target nonblack creature. It can't be regenerated.", '{T}, Mill a card: Add {C}. (To mill a card, put the top card of your library into your graveyard.)', "{T}, Mill a card: For each colored mana symbol in the milled card's mana cost, add one mana of that color. Activate only as an instant. (For example, if the card's mana cost is {3}{U}{U}{B}, you add {U}{U}{B}.)", '{T}, Sacrifice two lands and Sandstone Deadfall: Destroy target attacking creature.', '{T}: Add {B}. Cabal Pit deals 1 damage to you.\\nThreshold — {B}, {T}, Sacrifice Cabal Pit: Target creature gets -2/-2 until end of turn. Activate only if seven or more cards are in your graveyard.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{1}, {T}: Untap target land.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{5}, {T}: Add {W}{U}{B}{R}{G}.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}, Sacrifice Petrified Field: Return target land card from your graveyard to your hand.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Add one mana of any color. Tarnished Citadel deals 3 damage to you.', '{T}: Add {C}{G}.', '{T}: Add {G}. Centaur Garden deals 1 damage to you.\\nThreshold — {G}, {T}, Sacrifice Centaur Garden: Target creature gets +3/+3 until end of turn. Activate only if seven or more cards are in your graveyard.', '{T}: Add {G}.\\nThreshold — Werebear gets +3/+3 as long as seven or more cards are in your graveyard.', '{T}: Add {R}. Barbarian Ring deals 1 damage to you.\\nThreshold — {R}, {T}, Sacrifice Barbarian Ring: It deals 2 damage to any target. Activate only if seven or more cards are in your graveyard.', '{T}: Add {U}. Cephalid Coliseum deals 1 damage to you.\\nThreshold — {U}, {T}, Sacrifice Cephalid Coliseum: Target player draws three cards, then discards three cards. Activate only if seven or more cards are in your graveyard.', '{T}: Add {W}. Nomad Stadium deals 1 damage to you.\\nThreshold — {W}, {T}, Sacrifice Nomad Stadium: You gain 4 life. Activate only if seven or more cards are in your graveyard.', '{T}: Destroy target creature token.', '{T}: Prevent the next 2 damage that would be dealt to any target this turn.\\nThreshold — {T}: Prevent the next 4 damage that would be dealt to any target this turn. Activate only if seven or more cards are in your graveyard.', '{T}: Put a fuse counter on target creature.\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, put a fuse counter on each creature with a fuse counter on it.\\nWhenever a creature has four or more fuse counters on it, remove all fuse counters from it and destroy it. That creature deals 4 damage to its controller.', '{T}: Target player draws a card, then discards a card.', '{T}: Target player draws two cards, then discards two cards.', '{T}: Whipkeeper deals damage to target creature equal to the damage already dealt to it this turn.', '{U}, {T}: You may tap or untap target creature.', '{U}{U}: Tap target creature without flying.', '{W}, Sacrifice Dedicated Martyr: You gain 3 life.', '{W}, {T}: Tap target creature.\\nThreshold — {W}{W}, {T}: Tap two target creatures. Activate only if seven or more cards are in your graveyard.', '{W}, {T}: Target permanent you control gains protection from instant spells and from sorcery spells until end of turn.', '{W}: Luminous Guardian gets +0/+1 until end of turn.\\n{2}: Luminous Guardian can block an additional creature this turn.', '{X}: Testament of Faith becomes an X/X Wall creature with defender in addition to its other types until end of turn.']
flavor: ['"A life is measured by the lives it saves."', '"Amazing, isn\'t it, what humans will throw away when they\'re drowning?"', '"Any fool who would die for honor is better off dead."\\n—Cabal Patriarch', '"Anyone can admire creation. Only a barbarian sees the beauty in demolition."\\n—Kamahl, pit fighter', '"Anyone can snap her fingers and yank a soul. I prefer to kill creatively."\\n—Braids, dementia summoner', '"At the Reapportionment, Eagle begged to be human. The Ancestor granted half that prayer."\\n—Nomad myth', '"Belief in the Ancestor is admirable, but our enemies often demand something more . . . tangible."\\n—Pianna, nomad captain', '"Break one in half and you\'ll get a decent—if gooey—pair of weapons."\\n—Centaur warrior', '"Can you feel your instincts overwhelm your reason?"\\n—Watnik, master glassblower', '"Do you thirst for knowledge no matter the cost?"\\n—Watnik, master glassblower', '"Does your passion for power consume your soul?"\\n—Watnik, master glassblower', '"Doing okay back there, Tarv? Tarv?"', '"Don\'t dismiss its anger as mindless fury. I assure you, it has purpose."\\n—Seton, centaur druid', '"Finding the way once is luck. Finding the way twice takes a good map."', '"From the sea came all life, and to the sea it will return. The sooner the better."\\n—Emperor Aboshan', '"Getting people to do what you want is merely a matter of telling them what they want to hear."', '"Has your peaceful nature led you on a crusade?"\\n—Watnik, master glassblower', '"Have your dreams of a better society become an obsession?"\\n—Watnik, master glassblower', '"His strengths are pride, devotion, and ambition. His weaknesses are the same."\\n—Pianna, nomad captain', '"Holy couriers guide aven spirits up to the home of the Ancestor."\\n—Mystic elder', '"Home is where you can find a decent graveyard and strangers can disappear without awkward questions."', '"How tragic that greed eclipses beauty."\\n—Seton, centaur druid', '"I didn\'t come to play. I came to win."', '"I have a hunch we\'ll be seeing that one again soon."\\n—Ambassador Laquatus', '"I once saw a single barbarian charge a band of twenty nomads. I\'ve seen some crazy ones, too."\\n—Nomad sentry', '"I want a banana *this* big!"', '"I would die a thousand deaths before I let you harm another."', '"I\'m not sure which impresses me most, its thoroughness or its intensity."\\n—Matoc, lavamancer', '"I\'ve heard of putting the cat out, but this isn\'t what I had in mind."\\n—Nomad sentry', '"If he\'s so willing to suffer for his cause, then by all means, let us oblige him."\\n—Cabal Patriarch', '"If you don\'t hit your adversaries while they\'re down, they might get up again."', '"It offers you what you want, not what you need."\\n—Braids, dementia summoner', '"It\'s not really stealing. It\'s more like extended borrowing."', '"It\'s only frightened five people to death. Not my best work."\\n—Braids, dementia summoner', '"Let all we have buried be buried forever."\\n—Seton, centaur druid', '"Lizards make excellent familiars. They never know when they\'ve lost."\\n—Matoc, lavamancer', '"Memories can\'t simply be washed away. The mind must be scrubbed clean."\\n—Ambassador Laquatus', '"Nature is the endless dance between life and death."\\n—Seton, centaur druid', '"No mage\'s deception can harm those who keep nature balanced."', '"No one can fight the tide forever."', '"Not even my shadow knows where I am."', '"Pain teaches lessons no scholar can."\\n—Kamahl, pit fighter', '"Pound the steel until it fits. Doesn\'t work? Bash to bits."\\n—Dwarven forging song', '"Practice makes perfect, but obsession makes better."', '"Protocol demands that you bow down before me. I always stand on protocol."', '"Punch and drag, Toss the slag, Sift the soil, Leave the spoil."', '"Run away! It\'s an . . . um . . . run away!"\\n—Nomad sentry', '"Sheesh! How am I supposed to make a decent living around here?"\\n—Cabal grave robber', '"Survival of the fittest is not only the law of the pits, it is the law of nature. That is why I fight."', '"Take your time."', '"The Ancestor protects us in ways we can\'t begin to comprehend."\\n—Mystic elder', '"The animal spirits are the Ancestor\'s grandchildren. Remember them."\\n—Mystic elder', '"The aven are heralds of divinity. The greatest glory is to join them in the sky."', '"The best way to teach is by example."', '"The first birth celebrates life. The second birth mocks it."\\n—Mystic elder', '"The tiniest ripple tells a story ten fathoms deep."', '"The treasure in my mind is greater than any worldly glory."', '"The world has enough strife as it is. Where would we be if we turned against each other?"\\n—Pianna, nomad captain', '"There is no victory without virtue."', '"There is purity in all things. Even hatred."\\n—Lieutenant Kirtar', '"There will be gains for our losses. There will be rights for our wrongs."', '"There\'s dead, and then there\'s *dead* dead."\\n—Steamclaw driver', '"True strength lies in action. Let the weak react to me."\\n—Kamahl, pit fighter', '"Twisted magic, twisted fate, Force the land to ooze with hate."\\n—Cabal chant', '"Two or three tons of rock can really get you down—and keep you there."\\n—Kamahl, pit fighter', '"Victory in the pits is almost as rewarding as the methods I use to achieve it."', '"We\'ve survived starvation, dwarf attacks, and heatstroke. Why should a little sandstorm bother us?"', '"What\'s the fun of being a wizard if you can\'t mess with people\'s heads?"', '"With friends like these, who needs people?"', '"Your tenacity is admirable. And futile."\\n—Emperor Aboshan', '"Zombies don\'t kill. They recruit."\\n—Braids, dementia summoner', "A blossom's petals close inward to shut out the frost.\\n—Nantuko teaching", 'A finely crafted blade will never meet as many blows on the battlefield as it did on the anvil.', 'A good memory is no match for a good scribe.', 'A grave is the safest place to store ill-gotten treasures.', 'A leaf dancer sweeps through the forest like a spring breeze, evading even the sharpest eyes and ears.', 'A monument to long-forgotten gods, it stands as a tribute to the fleeting nature of human ways.', 'After the invasion devastated the Talruum and Hurloon tribes, the survivors began to search for other minotaurs.', 'Aimed by the eyes of eagles, their arrows never miss the mark.', 'An army of squirrels is still an army.', 'Any given foothill may hide dozens of dwarves waiting to spill from their tunnels like fire ants.', "As fleeting as a cephalid's promise.", "As haunting as a zombie's curse.", "As hot as a dwarf's rage.", "As strong as a centaur's will.", "As uplifting as a mystic's dreams.", 'Balshan wizards have long used them to gnaw away the memories they wish to forget.', 'Barbarians equate courage with the ability to endure pain.', 'Beauty stirs the memory like a sweet perfume excites the air.', 'Books are like crops—they must be thinned for best yield.', 'Cephalids seek knowledge not to better themselves, but to best others.', 'Cephalids specialize in things unseen, be they politics, betrayal, or themselves.', 'Cephalids value the free exchange of ideas—except for the "free" part.', 'Cephalids whisper flattery in your ear, put jewels in your hand, spin dreams in your head, and stick knives in your back.', 'Crian\'s patrols afford him plenty of opportunity to take potshots at the "dirtwalkers" far below.', 'Death is a moth that dances toward our inner flame. The brightest fire can singe its wings.\\n—Nantuko teaching', 'Dreads had half a mind to leave.', 'Duty subdues instinct.', 'Dwarves have been known to take pickaxes to their own creations, hoping to discover treasures within.', 'Even the trivial can inspire.', "Faster than a cobra's bite.", "For sale: Complete wizard's library. Rare scrolls, grimoires, and works of ancient spellcrafting! Slightly abridged.", 'From Otaria, the sun above meets the sea below at a glittering horizon.', 'Good strategists seize opportunities. Great strategists make their own.', 'Grace repels darkness.', 'Hard as stone and twice as stubborn.\\n—Dwarven compliment', 'He exercises his right to bear arms.', 'Her eyes blaze with the strength of twenty shields. Every glance is a salvation.', 'His feet buckled the ground, his hands cut the wind to ribbons, and he was gone.', "His quiet words fade into the night's chill, yet they burn into his listeners' minds with all the power of a thousand suns.", 'His reputation precedes him—and so does his weapon.', "If you can take something from a nomad, it's probably bait.", "Imps aren't born knowing how to fly—just how to annoy.", 'In a world still pained from burns, some are born already scarred.', "In the Krosan Forest, you've got to keep an eye out for the squirrels.", 'In the gardens of the centaurs, many travelers have mysteriously vanished while admiring the elaborate topiaries.', 'It *is* the thing that goes bump in the night.', 'It despises humans and squirrels and beasts and dwarves and cephalids . . . well, it despises just about everything.', 'It glides through the shadows until it reaches yours.', 'It helps to have an extra direction in which to run.', 'It lurks in the mist, waiting for stragglers to fall behind. When the fog clears, nothing remains but footprints.', 'It relishes old-fashioned family meals.', 'It suddenly dawned on Jorin that farming was quite a noble profession.', 'It takes a remarkable cleric to turn a group of healers into a hospital.', 'It teaches *you* to play dead.', "It's important to face your inner demons . . . unless they're the kind of demons that can kill you.", 'Just as each added feather steadies the wing, so does the flock grow stronger with each new member.', "Knowledge can't be kept in a bottle or sealed in a box. It yearns to be spread and shared.", 'Lavamancers make simple requests: obey or die.', 'Law smothers anarchy.', 'Lush growth spreads like a ferocious blaze across the Otarian hillsides.', 'Memories have distinct tastes. Its favorites are the sickly sweetness of lost love and the bitter smokiness of cruel murder.', 'Murky Otarian tides hide the forgotten treacheries of the Phyrexian war.', 'Near the Krosan border, farmers keep watch over their fields lest the sod get up and wander away.', 'Nomad and Nantuko, eagle and elephant; all the birds and beasts are charmed by his quiet dignity.', 'Nomad youths aspire to one of two roles in the tribe: priest or warrior. Their secret dream is to become both.', 'Nomads understand many cultures and therefore travel without fear.', 'Nothing is sacred to the undead—not even their own kind.', "Oddly, no one questioned the Cabal's wisdom in hiring a zombie to work at the cemetery.", 'On Otaria, peace and harmony are rare. Places that provide both are cherished.', 'One never knows when inspiration will bubble up.', "Only a handful have seen it transform. Or, from the wurm's perspective, only a mouthful.", "Otaria's frequent tremors are the last stages of Dominaria's recovery from the Phyrexian war.", 'Plant a field with wishes, and you will grow more wishes.\\n—Nantuko teaching', 'Politics is just a subtle form of mind control—and cephalids are master politicians.', 'Reach out and torch someone.', 'Reason exposes deception.', 'Scribbles of a lunatic and formulas of a genius are often indistinguishable.', 'She enraptures all, encompasses all, endures all.', "She'd have a fearsome reputation if she left any survivors.", "Slow and steady may not always win the race, but at least it doesn't end up splattered on the walls.", 'Some find inspiration in their swords. Others find it in their leaders.', "Some things even fleas won't bite.", "Sometimes destruction is Dominaria's way of rebuilding. Sometimes it's not.", 'Sometimes you have to read between the minds.', 'Spot one ember beast, attack.\\nSpot a second, best fall back.\\n—Dwarven saying', 'Spreading a blanket of growth to warm a weary world.', 'Standing near a volcano\\n—Barbarian expression meaning "asking for it"', 'Suffer the little creatures, for they may yet rise up and beat you senseless.', 'That which grows without roots cannot be uprooted.\\n—Nantuko teaching', 'The Pardic Mountains are known for their spicy cuisine.', 'The aven claim it feeds on thunder and rainbows.', 'The best ideas often come from the worst minds.', 'The best thing about ogres is that they never try to sneak up on you.', 'The bones it buries may be yours.', 'The calm comes after the storm.', 'The carnage of conflicts long past still stains the Otarian soil.', "The centaurs' simple magic can undo a basilisk's gaze, but only for a short time.", 'The courageous accomplish more in a single moment than the cowardly do in a lifetime.', 'The dance of angry feet\\n—Nantuko expression meaning "stampede"', 'The druids and the forest are in perfect harmony. They sing the same songs.', 'The first memory it sucks out of its host is how to get rid of it.', "The fondest memories burn brightest. As they're lost forever, the flames grow hotter still.", "The gems' incandescence invades the dreams of all who see them.", 'The ground trembled in a violent purr.', 'The more they survey the dreadful dry expanses, the more the cephalids thirst to tame them.', 'The more unlikely the victory, the more memorable the success.', 'The most popular pit fighters are brought back for encore performances.', "The nomads' funeral pyres are more practical than ceremonial.", 'The pits feed both its thirst for combat and its thirst for blood.', 'The pits swallow the weak as predators swallow prey.', 'The relationship between hunter and hunted knows nothing of alliances.', 'The same spears that catch their food today will defend their homes tomorrow.', 'The scrape of shovels and the tumble of cold dirt soon muffled their pleas.', 'The toymaker frowned in bewilderment. None of his creations had ever sneezed before.', 'The wizard who reads a thousand books is powerful. The wizard who memorizes a thousand books is insane.', 'Their whispered prayers rally the nomads better than any war cry could.', "There's lots of time like the present.", "There's no such thing as a little bit of lava.", 'Thinking is hard.', "Those who follow nature's path eventually walk in a circle.", "Those who see the squirrels go underground in the winter aren't ready for what emerges in the spring.", 'Those who will not follow are doomed to lead.', 'To say Nixar had a splitting headache would be a bit of an understatement.', 'To the camp, it was a fierce and loyal protector. To the sentry\'s youngest daughter, it would always be her "Wuv Muffin."', 'To treat flesh wounds, use earth. To treat earth wounds, use flesh.\\n—Barbarian saying', 'To unearth its dinner, it inters itself.', 'Truth tempers fanaticism.', 'Unanswered prayers are themselves answers.\\n—Nantuko teaching', 'What is a tree? Slow hard thought. What is a flower? Swift soft flesh. What is a druid? Both.', "When building gnomes, dwarves adhere to the highest standards. The gnomes themselves aren't as particular.", 'When in doubt, stomp.', "When one of the Patriarch's champions displeased him, he would only shake his finger. That was enough.", 'When the crimson fades from the magical embers, a final wisp of smoke will rise. Soon after, hostilities will begin anew.', 'Wracked with rot, it wrecks and ruins.', 'Zombies mourn for the living and celebrate those who will soon be given the gift of death.']
artist: ['Adam Rex', 'Alan Pollack', 'Alex Horley-Orlandelli', 'Anthony S. Waters', 'Arnie Swekel', 'Ben Thompson', 'Bob Petillo', 'Bradley Williams', 'Brian Snõddy', 'Carl Critchlow', 'Christopher Moeller', 'Ciruelo', 'Clyde Caldwell', 'D. Alexander Gregory', 'Dany Orizio', 'Daren Bader', 'Darrell Riche', 'Dave Dorman', 'David Martin', 'Don Hazeltine', 'Donato Giancola', 'Edward P. Beard, Jr.', 'Eric Peterson', 'Franz Vohwinkel', 'Gary Ruddell', 'Glen Angus', 'Glen Angus & Arnie Swekel', 'Greg Hildebrandt & Tim Hildebrandt', 'Greg Staples', 'Heather Hudson', 'Jeff Remmer', 'Jerry Tiritilli', 'Jim Nelson', 'John Avon', 'John Matson', 'Justin Sweet', 'Keith Garletts', 'Kev Walker', 'Larry Elmore', 'Luca Zontini', 'Marc Fishman', 'Mark Brill', 'Mark Romanoski', 'Mark Tedin', 'Mark Zug', 'Massimilano Frezzato', 'Matt Cavotta', 'Mike Ploog', 'Monte Michael Moore', 'Paolo Parente', 'Pete Venters', 'Ray Lago', 'Rebecca Guay', 'Rick Farrell', 'Rob Alexander', 'Roger Raupp', 'Ron Spears', 'Ron Spencer', 'Scott M. Fischer', 'Terese Nielsen', 'Thomas M. Baxa', 'Tony Szczudlo', 'Wayne England', 'rk post']
